# oracle: reset_atoms id sort yes on a shuffled 24-atom angle system (w143cf_reset_sort.data: IDs and storage order
#   shuffled, 16 bonds, 6 angles, box -4.5..4.5). Native LAMMPS (src/reset_atoms_id.cpp at b332f28, sort(): bins of
#   binsize = (vol / (natoms/10 + 1))^(1/dim) over the bounding box grown by 1e-4 of its length; new IDs go in bin order
#   (z-block, then y, then x), then by x, y, z inside a bin; sort_bins() numbers them 1..N). The bonded and angle
#   topology is renumbered; write_data writes the result (ids, positions, bonds, angles) and is compared with the native file.
#   Measured with native LAMMPS.
#   Engine vs native (fixture): IDs and positions identical; the derived bin order matched all 24 atoms before the engine was written.
# oracle-inputs: w143cf_reset_sort.data
# oracle-files: w143cf_reset_sort.written.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-12 abs=1e-14
units           lj
atom_style      angle
read_data       w143cf_reset_sort.data
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 0.0 1.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 1.0 1.0
angle_style     harmonic
angle_coeff     1 1.0 109.0
reset_atoms     id sort yes
thermo_style    custom step pe
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
write_data      w143cf_reset_sort.written.data
